<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jalingo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jalingo is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taraba-state">Taraba State</a>, created in 1991. It became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of Muri in the 1890s, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of Muri still resides there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jalingo.jpg" alt="Jalingo" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rbutso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modern_Jalingo_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
